00:46:41.260 --> 00:46:43.520
and helpful and just wanted to get it done right.

945
00:46:44.360 --> 00:46:48.500
Except, I think, Brian and Ed, who were just trying to make me laugh the whole time.

946
00:46:49.160 --> 00:46:53.620
Can I say, Angela, that when we got these audio clips from Paul, the thing that was so

947
00:46:53.620 --> 00:47:02.800
fun for me was his observations as a non-actor being on a set, because it really took me back

948
00:47:02.800 --> 00:47:08.700
to all of those moments in my career as an actor where you just are learning on the fly.

949
00:47:08.980 --> 00:47:11.580
I didn't learn any of this stuff in theater school.

